# Copy this file to .env.local (Vite loads it automatically, and it's git-ignored)
# to enable cloud backup to Google Drive and/or Yandex Disk. Leave a value empty
# to keep that provider hidden/disabled in Settings — the app works fine without
# either of them, cloud backup is purely optional.

# Google Drive backup.
# 1. Create a project at https://console.cloud.google.com/ and enable the
#    "Google Drive API".
# 2. Under "APIs & Services -> Credentials", create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID of
#    type "Web application".
# 3. Add this app's URL (e.g. https://<owner>.github.io/my-car/ and
#    http://localhost:5173/ for local dev) under "Authorized JavaScript origins".
# 4. Paste the Client ID below. Only the drive.appdata scope is requested — the
#    app can only see the single backup file it creates, never the rest of the
#    user's Drive.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Yandex Disk backup.
# 1. Register an app at https://oauth.yandex.ru/client/new, platform
#    "Веб-сервисы".
# 2. Add this app's URL (e.g. https://<owner>.github.io/my-car/ and
#    http://localhost:5173/ for local dev) as a "Redirect URI" — it must match
#    exactly, including the trailing slash.
# 3. Grant the scopes "Яндекс.Диск REST API: доступ к папке приложения"
#    (cloud_api:disk.app_folder) and "доступ к информации о диске"
#    (cloud_api:disk.info).
# 4. Paste the Client ID below.
VITE_YANDEX_CLIENT_ID=
